I told you, didn't I?

140
00:08:47,180 --> 00:08:50,097
Sub-zero temperatures bring
everything in the area to a halt.

141
00:08:50,180 --> 00:08:52,945
Gases become liquids and
liquids become solids.

142
00:08:53,300 --> 00:08:54,680
Look a little closer.

143
00:08:54,940 --> 00:08:56,700
See the suspended vapor now?

144
00:08:56,900 --> 00:08:59,060
It's a bullet, Mista! That sound!

145
00:08:59,240 --> 00:09:00,887
It was a ricocheting bullet!

146
00:09:01,100 --> 00:09:02,900
Get out of the way! What?

147
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:06,080
That's White Ice's ability.

148
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:07,920
It's called Gently Weeps.

149
00:09:09,220 --> 00:09:12,200
I'd already created a
frozen barrier of vapor.

150
00:09:12,540 --> 00:09:14,997
Sure, it takes a lot of
energy to make it work,

151
00:09:15,080 --> 00:09:17,177
but it protects me from
just about anything?

152
00:09:17,260 --> 00:09:19,457
including your damn bolts and bullets.

153
00:09:19,540 --> 00:09:21,940
I'm protected by a barrier of stasis.

154
00:09:22,140 --> 00:09:25,140
I have you to thank for
that little trick, Mista.

155
00:09:26,220 --> 00:09:28,102
Jonah's prediction was right on.

156
00:09:28,720 --> 00:09:30,000
This is my fault.

157
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:31,700
Endless charge.

158
00:09:32,540 --> 00:09:35,952
Why didn't I go after that
stupid disc from the beginning?

159
00:09:37,920 --> 00:09:40,237
It's not on your benches or in the trash.

160
00:09:40,320 --> 00:09:42,496
I know it wouldn't be in plain sight,

161
00:09:42,620 --> 00:09:46,091
but there's nothing around here
that even resembles a disc.

162
00:09:46,360 --> 00:09:49,242
Considering how eager
Mista was to get over here,

163
00:09:49,420 --> 00:09:52,302
I'm sure the hiding spot
must be pretty close by.

164
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:53,840
Where is it?

165
00:09:54,220 --> 00:09:56,220
